{"subjectId":"dsa-advanced","id":"hashing","title":"Hashing","group":"","order":7,"html":"<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> a[] = [10, 15, 20, 5, 20] ; b[] = [30, 5, 30, 80]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2</p>\n</div>\n<p>1 - Initialize res = 0</p>\n<p>2 - Traverse through Every Element of a[]</p>\n<p> 2.1 - Check if it has not appeared already</p>\n<p> 2.2 - If a new element and also present in b[], do res++</p>\n<p>3 - return res</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef countUniqueInAAlsoInB(a, b):\n    res = 0\n    b_set = set(b)\n    seen = set()\n\n    for element in a:\n        if element not in seen:\n            if element in b_set:\n                res += 1\n            seen.add(element)\n\n    return res\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nb = [3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(countUniqueInAAlsoInB(a, b))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2\n\ndef intersection(arr1, m, arr2, n):\n  res = 0\n  for i in range(i-1):\n    flag = False\n    for j in range(i-1):\n      if arr1[j] == arr1[i]:\n        flag = True\n        break\n\n    if flag == True:\n      continue\n\n    for j in range(n):\n      if arr[i] == arr2[j]:\n        res += 1\n        break\n\n  return res\n\narr1 = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\narr2 = [3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(intersection(arr1, len(arr1), arr2, len(arr2)))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution 1\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nb = [3, 4, 5, 6, 7]\n\n\ns_a = set(a)\ns_b = set(b)\n\ncount = 0\nfor element in s_a:\n    if element in s_b:\n        count += 1\n\nprint(count)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution 2\n\ndef intersection(arr1, m, arr2, n):\n  us = set()\n  for i in range(m):\n    us.add(arr1[i])\n\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    if arr2[i] in us:\n      res += 1\n      us.remove(arr2[i])\n\n  return res\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nb = [3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(intersection(a, len(a), b, len(b)))</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Union of Two unsorted Arrays</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> a[] = [15, 20, 5, 15] ; b[] = [15, 15, 15, 20, 10]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 4</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef unionSet(arr1, m, arr2, n):\n  c = [0]*(m+n)\n\n  for i in range(m):\n    c[i] = arr1[i]\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    c[m+i] = arr2[i]\n\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in range(m+n):\n    flag = False\n    for j in range(i):\n      if c[i] == c[j]:\n        flag = True\n        break\n    if flag == False:\n      res += 1\n\n  return res\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nb = [3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(unionSet(a, len(a), b, len(b)))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(m+n)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef unionSet(arr1, m, arr2, n):\n  us = set()\n  for i in arr1:\n    us.add(i)\n\n  for i in arr2:\n    us.add(i)\n\n  return len(us)\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nb = [3, 4, 5, 6]\nprint(unionSet(a, len(a), b, len(b)))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(m+n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Pair with Given Sum</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [3, 2, 8, 15, -18] ; sum = 17<br><strong>Output:</strong> True<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [2, 1, 6, 3] ; sum = 6<br><strong>Output:</strong> False</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef pairwithSum(arr, x):\n  for i in range(len(arr)):\n    for j in range(i+1, len(arr)):\n      if arr[i] + arr[j] == x:\n        return True\n\n  return False\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nsum = 7\npairwithSum(a, sum)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef pairwithSum(arr, x):\n  us = set()\n\n  for i in arr:\n    if x-i in us:\n      return True\n    us.add(i)\n\n  return False\n\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nsum = 7\npairwithSum(a, sum)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Subarray with 0 Sum</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]<br><strong>Output:</strong> False<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr = [-1, 4, -3, 5, 1]<br><strong>Output:</strong> True</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef isZero(l):\n  n = len(l)\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i+1, n+1):\n      if sum(l[i:j]) == 0:\n        return True\n\n  return False\n\n\na = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 5]\nisZero(a)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef isZero(l):\n  preSum = 0\n  h = set()\n\n  for i in range(len(l)):\n    preSum += l[i]\n\n    if preSum == 0 or preSum in h:\n      return True\n\n    h.add(preSum)\n\n  return False\n\n\na = [1, -2, -3, 5, 2, 4, 5]\nisZero(a)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check for Palindrome Permutation</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"geek\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> False<br><strong>Input:</strong> \"geegg\"<br><strong>Output:</strong> True || gegeg or eggge</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\nfrom itertools import permutations\n\ndef is_palindrome(s):\n    return s == s[::-1]\n\ndef check(s):\n    perms = permutations(s)\n\n    for perm in perms:\n        if is_palindrome(''.join(perm)):\n            return True\n\n    return False\n\ns1 = \"geek\"\ns2 = \"geegg\"\n\nprint(check(s1))\nprint(check(s2))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef isPalper(s):\n  cnt = Counter(s)\n  odd = 0\n\n  for freq in cnt.values():\n    if freq % 2 != 0:\n      odd = odd + 1\n\n      if odd &gt; 1:\n        return False\n\n  return True\n\ns = \"ggegg\"\nisPalper(s)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Longest Subarray with Sum</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [5, 8, -4, -4, 9, -2, 2] ; sum = 0<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [3, 1, 0, 1, 8, 2, 3, 6] ; sum = 5<br><strong>Output:</strong> 4</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef longestSubarray(arr, sum):\n  n = len(arr)\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    curr_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i, n):\n      curr_sum += arr[j]\n\n      if curr_sum == sum:\n        res = max(res, j-i+1)\n\n  return res\n\narr = [5, 8, -4, -4, 9, -2, 2]\nsum = 0\nlongestSubarray(arr, sum)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef longest(arr, sum):\n  n = len(arr)\n  mydict = dict()\n  pre_sum = 0\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    pre_sum += arr[i]\n\n    if pre_sum == sum:\n      res = i + 1\n\n    if pre_sum not in mydict:\n      mydict[pre_sum] = i\n\n    if pre_sum - sum in mydict:\n      res = max(res, i-mydict[pre_sum - sum])\n\n  return res\n\narr = [5, 8, -4, -4, 9, -2, 2]\nsum = 0\nlongest(arr, sum)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Longest Subarray with equal no.of zero and One</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def findSubArray(arr, n):\n    maxsize = -1\n    startindex = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        sum = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            sum += -1 if arr[j] == 0 else 1\n\n            if sum == 0 and (j - i + 1) &gt; maxsize:\n                maxsize = j - i + 1\n                startindex = i\n\n    if maxsize == -1:\n        print(\"No such subarray\")\n    else:\n        print(startindex, \"to\", startindex + maxsize - 1)\n\n    return maxsize\n\narr = [1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1]\nsize = len(arr)\nprint(findSubArray(arr, size))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef largest(arr):\n  n = len(arr)\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    if arr[i] == 0:\n      arr[i] = -1\n\n  mydict = dict()\n  sum = 0\n  maxlen = 0\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    sum += arr[i]\n\n    if sum == 0:\n      maxlen = i + 1\n\n    if sum in mydict:\n      maxlen = max(maxlen, i-mydict[sum])\n    else:\n      mydict[sum] = i\n\n  return maxlen\n\narr = [1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1]\nprint(largest(arr))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Longest Common Subarray with Given Sum</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr1[] = [0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0] ; arr2[] = [1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 4<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr1[] = [0, 0, 0] ; arr2 = [1, 1, 1]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 0</p>\n</div>\n<p> we are giving two binary subarrays of same size</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef longest(arr1, arr2):\n  res = 0\n  n = len(arr1)\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    sum1 = 0\n    sum2 = 0\n\n    for j in range(i, n):\n      sum1 += arr1[j]\n      sum2 += arr2[j]\n\n      if sum1 == sum2:\n        res = max(res, j-i+1)\n\n  return res\n\narr1 = [0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0]\narr2 = [1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1]\nlongest(arr1, arr2)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def longest(arr1, arr2):\n    n = len(arr1)\n\n    # Create a new array where each element is the difference between arr1 and arr2\n    arr = [arr1[i] - arr2[i] for i in range(n)]\n\n    # Dictionary to store the first occurrence of each cumulative sum\n    mydict = {}\n    sum = 0\n    max_len = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        sum += arr[i]\n\n        # If the cumulative sum is zero, it means the subarray from the start to the current index is valid\n        if sum == 0:\n            max_len = i + 1\n\n        # If the cumulative sum has been seen before, update the max_len\n        if sum in mydict:\n            max_len = max(max_len, i - mydict[sum])\n        else:\n            # Store the first occurrence of this cumulative sum\n            mydict[sum] = i\n\n    return max_len\n\narr1 = [0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0]\narr2 = [1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1]\nprint(longest(arr1, arr2))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Longest Consecutive SubSequence</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> a[] = [1, 9, 3, 4, 2, 20]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 4<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [8, 20, 7, 30]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [20, 30, 40]<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1</p>\n</div>\n<p>We need to find the longest subsequence in the form of x, x + 1, x + 2, x + 3 ......... x + i with these elements appearing in any order</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef findLong(arr):\n  n = len(arr)\n  arr.sort()\n  res = 1\n  curr = 1\n\n  for i in range(1, n):\n    if arr[i] == arr[i-1] + 1:\n      curr += 1\n    else:\n      res = max(res, curr)\n      curr = 1\n\n  res = max(res, curr)\n\n  return res\n\narr = [1, 9, 3, 4, 2, 20]\nfindLong(arr)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n'''\nWe first insert all elements in a hash table. Then with 2n lookups, we find the result\n\narr[] = {1, 3, 4, 3, 3, 2, 9, 10}\nh = {1, 3, 4, 2, 9, 10}\n'''\n\ndef findLong(arr):\n  s = set()\n  res = 0\n\n  for i in arr:\n    s.add(i)\n\n  for i in arr:\n    if (i-1) not in s:\n      curr = 1\n\n      while (curr + i) in s:\n        curr += 1\n\n      res = max(res, curr)\n\n  return res\n\narr = [1, 9, 3, 4, 2, 20]\nfindLong(arr)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Count Distinct Elements in Every Window</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr = [10, 20, 20, 10, 30, 40, 10] ; k = 4<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2 3 4 3<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr = [10, 20, 30, 40] ; k = 3<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3 3</p>\n</div>\n<h4>Idea for Naive Solution Algorithm</h4>\n<p>1) There will be (n-k+1) windows</p>\n<p>2) There through every window and count distinct elements in it</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef printDis(arr, k):\n  n = len(arr)\n  for i in range(n - k + 1):\n    print(len(set(arr[i : i +k ])))\n\narr = [10, 20, 20, 10, 30, 40, 10]\nk = 4\nprintDis(arr, k)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\n# The Idea is to use count of previous window to get the current count\n\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef countDis(arr, k):\n  mp = Counter(arr[0:k])\n  print(len(mp))\n\n  for i in range(k, len(arr)):\n    x = arr[i-k]\n    mp[x] -= 1\n    mp[arr[i]] += 1\n\n    if mp[x] == 0:\n      del mp[x]\n\n    print(len(mp))\n\narr = [10, 20, 20, 10, 30, 40, 10]\nk = 4\ncountDis(arr, k)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(k)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>More than n/k Occurrences</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [30, 10, 20, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30] ; k = 4<br><strong>Output:</strong> 20 30</p>\n</div>\n<p>Note : n = 8, n/k = 8/4 = 2 : Occurrences more than</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef NbyK(arr, k):\n  arr.sort()\n  i = 1\n  count = 1\n  n = len(arr)\n\n  while i &lt; len(arr):\n    while i &lt; len(arr) and arr[i] == arr[i-1]:\n      count += 1\n      i += 1\n\n    if count &gt; n//k:\n      print(arr[i-1], end = \" \")\n\n    count = 1\n    i = i + 1\n\narr = [30, 10, 20, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30]\nk = 4\nNbyK(arr, k)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef NbyK(arr, k):\n  c = Counter(arr)\n  n = len(arr)\n\n  for x in c:\n    if c[x] &gt; n//k:\n      print(x, end = \" \")\n\narr = [30, 10, 20, 20, 10, 20, 30, 30]\nk = 4\nNbyK(arr, k)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>More than n/k Occurences</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def more_than_n_by_k(arr, n, k):\n\n    m = {}\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if arr[i] in m:\n            m[arr[i]] += 1\n        elif len(m) &lt; k - 1:\n            m[arr[i]] = 1\n        else:\n            keys_to_remove = []\n            for key in m:\n                m[key] -= 1\n                if m[key] == 0:\n                    keys_to_remove.append(key)\n\n            for key in keys_to_remove:\n                del m[key]\n\n    for key in m.keys():\n        m[key] = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if arr[i] in m:\n            m[arr[i]] += 1\n\n    result = []\n    for key, count in m.items():\n        if count &gt; n // k:\n            result.append(key)\n\n    return result\n\narr = [3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 3, 3]\nn = len(arr)\nk = 4\nprint(more_than_n_by_k(arr, n, k))</code></pre></figure></section>"}